# Tracks (owner 2026-09-17): "depending on terrain foot and track prints should be
# left behind player". Boots walked across the grounds that keep a print, the
# growth that only bends, and a run through snow. Every ground is found by name: a
# landscape first, then the ground in it (sand is walked in
# tests/tracks/test_tracks_in_game.gd: this island's shore is too narrow a strip for
# a tour to stand on).
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/tracks.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
zoom 6
place snowfield
ground snow
wait 0.8
walk 1,0 1.6
wait 0.4
await tracks:snow 3
shot 01-boot-prints-in-snow with tracks:snow
zoom 3
wait 0.6
shot 02-the-snow-prints-close with tracks:snow
zoom 6
place burning
ground ash
wait 0.8
walk 0,-1 1.6
wait 0.4
await tracks:ash 3
shot 03-prints-in-ash with tracks:ash
# The PEAT is the moss's own ground, not the border's: staged at the
# moss-bonelands ecotone this asked for mud or peat where the ground can be all
# bonelands, and found none within reach on seed 1 -- measured failing at the
# identical tile at b05fb46, so it predates both the worldgen move and the
# tracks warm-up. Aimed at the moss itself; the claim below is unchanged.
place moss
ground mud,peat
wait 0.8
walk 0,1 1.6
wait 0.4
await tracks:foot 3
shot 04-prints-in-the-peat with tracks:mud|tracks:peat
place salt_flats
ground salt
wait 0.8
walk -1,0 1.6
wait 0.4
await tracks:salt 3
shot 05-prints-on-the-salt with tracks:salt
place spawn
ground grass
wait 0.8
walk -1,0 1.6
wait 0.4
await tracks:flatten 3
shot 06-grass-bent-down-behind with tracks:flatten
# Nine world hours on: every print of the day worn away or filled in, even the
# peat's, which holds a print eight hours and not a minute more.
hour 19
until no_tracks 4
wait 0.4
shot 07-by-evening-nothing-left-of-them with no_tracks
